{"id": "EUVD-2026-102280", "enisaUuid": "9bfd79e0-ed8f-3c1f-ac1f-93e7563c9938", "description": "Game Music Emu (libgme) through 0.6.5 contains a global out-of-bounds read vulnerability in Classic_Emu::mute_voices_ that allows attackers to crash applications by supplying NSF files whose voice count exceeds the 16-entry voice-type table. Attackers can craft an NSF header with chip_flags 0x3F, opened through gme_open_data or gme_open_file, to read past the static array during loading and cause denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:42:42", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libgme-ay-track-table-underflow-oob-read", "https://github.com/libgme/game-music-emu/blob/9e23d10f9fd2a6a2f33b10912dd8dc7153258995/gme/Nsf_Emu.cpp#L212-L218", "https://github.com/libgme/game-music-emu/blob/9e23d10f9fd2a6a2f33b10912dd8dc7153258995/gme/Classic_Emu.cpp#L66-L80", "https://github.com/libgme/game-music-emu/issues/164", "https://github.com/libgme/game-music-emu", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/game-music-emu-libgme-through-0.6.5-out-of-bounds-read-via-classic-emu-mute-voices"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111153", "GHSA-9f4r-v8r3-c47c"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e62f0cba-3867-38ab-8dc3-e1c66c8ac571", "product": {"name": "game-music-emu", "vendor": {"name": "libgme"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.6.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e4b5b118-d4b3-339b-be2d-b0e9d1be88ca", "vendor": {"name": "libgme"}}], "isExploited": false}